Welcome to Google Cloud Shell, a tool for managing resources hosted on Google Cloud Platform!
The machine comes pre-installed with the Google Cloud SDK and other popular developer tools.

Your 5GB home directory will persist across sessions, but the VM is ephemeral and will be reset
approximately 20 minutes after your session ends. No system-wide change will persist beyond that.

Type "gcloud help" to get help on using Cloud SDK. For more examples, visit
https://cloud.google.com/shell/docs/quickstart and https://cloud.google.com/shell/docs/examples

Type "cloudshell help" to get help on using the "cloudshell" utility.  Common functionality is
aliased to short commands in your shell, for example, you can type "dl <filename>" at Bash prompt to
download a file. Type "cloudshell aliases" to see these commands.

Type "help" to see this message any time. Type "builtin help" to see Bash interpreter help.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #1e1e1e;
            color: #d4d4d4;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }
        .header {
            color: #f44336;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #444;
            padding-bottom: 5px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .step-box {
            background-color: #3a1d1d;
            border-left: 4px solid #f44336;
            padding: 15px;
            margin: 15px 0;
        }
        .instruction {
            color: #dcdcaa;
        }
        .highlight {
            color: #ce9178;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-family: monospace;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="header">CRITICAL SYNC ERROR DETECTED</div>

    <div class="step-box">
        <p class="instruction"><strong>Why nothing is working:</strong> Your current UI context shows that while you have a Project ID, the <span class="highlight">DISPLAY_NAME</span> is set to <strong>"None"</strong>.</p>
        <p class="instruction"><strong>Status:</strong> <span class="highlight">Project ID: noble-beanbag-497411-m4</span> | <span class="highlight">Display Name: None</span></p>

        <p>This means the Assistant is "blind" to your actual resources because the project isn't fully initialized in the active session. This causes the "Thinking..." hang and the missing buttons.</p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>To fix this immediately:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Go to the top bar of the Google Cloud Console.</li>
        <li>Click the <strong>Project Dropdown</strong> (next to the "Google Cloud" logo).</li>
        <li>Select the project <span class="highlight">noble-beanbag-497411-m4</span> manually, even if it looks like it's already selected.</li>
        <li>Refresh your browser tab.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>I am a BigQuery and Google Cloud specialist. Once that project name shows up instead of "None", I can generate the SQL or Python code you need. <strong>What is the code you are trying to write?</strong></p>

</body>
</html>

